1
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:11,667
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:33,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,733 --> 00:00:41,167
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:43,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:44,833
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:44,967 --> 00:00:46,400
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:51,533
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:53,500
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:55,567
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,833
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,967 --> 00:00:59,867
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:02,733
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:11,433
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:12,867
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:21,233
<i>I was telling them
how I got even more blessings</i>

21
00:01:21,367 --> 00:01:23,567
<i>ever since I purchased
Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

22
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:27,300
<i>Those informal settlers
will have to leave that place!</i>

23
00:01:27,433 --> 00:01:29,000
<i> They robbed Salvador.</i>

24
00:01:29,133 --> 00:01:30,933
Clearly, that idiot got bolder!

25
00:01:31,067 --> 00:01:32,733
<i>And there's the man
who saved me.</i>

26
00:01:32,867 --> 00:01:34,267
<i> He was so brave, boss!</i>

27
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,500
<i>This is so good.
We can use this!</i>

28
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:40,833
<i>Find the man who
went up against Paquito's men.</i>

29
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,933
Well, Gabo here wanted to treat
<i> us to some food and drinks.</i>

30
00:01:44,067 --> 00:01:45,367
<i>But since we were
with these three,</i>

31
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:46,533
<i> we got in trouble.</i>

32
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:48,533
<i>Why'd you have to work
for Gabo's enemy?</i>

33
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:51,367
<i> I'm so sick of being poor!</i>

34
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,833
<i>If that's what you want,
then suit yourself!</i>

35
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:57,933
What could
they be fighting about?

36
00:01:58,067 --> 00:02:00,167
Uncle Rudy also sounds mad.

37
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,667
Sounds pretty intense.

38
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,600
Maybe it's about Betchay
working at Paquito's bar.

39
00:02:05,733 --> 00:02:07,900
Why would Betchay work there?

40
00:02:08,033 --> 00:02:09,000
What a shame.

41
00:02:09,133 --> 00:02:11,833
Ma, don't say that.
Aunt Betchay might hear you.

42
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:13,033
She might come for us.

43
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:14,267
Oh, why? It's true.

44
00:02:14,433 --> 00:02:16,133
Hold up.
Watch your words, Aunt Diday.

45
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:17,733
My Grandma works there too.

46
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:18,667
It's the truth.

47
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:19,933
You know what's odd?

48
00:02:20,067 --> 00:02:22,567
Aunt Betchay got hired
at Paquito's bar.

49
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:24,433
Django is Gabo's enemy.

50
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:25,433
That smells like trouble.

51
00:02:25,567 --> 00:02:27,000
This I know for sure.

52
00:02:28,033 --> 00:02:31,567
Uncle Paquito and Django
will get back at Gabo

53
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:32,633
through Aunt Betchay.

54
00:02:32,767 --> 00:02:34,233
I knew them too well.

55
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:36,200
I know how their minds work.
I'm sure of it.

56
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:38,433
Let's just ignore them.
We might get dragged too.

57
00:02:38,567 --> 00:02:39,533
[TOLITS] Oh, she's coming.

58
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:42,067
[LAUGHTER, OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

59
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,700
That's funny!

60
00:02:43,833 --> 00:02:47,733
Of course, we're just
talking about food...

61
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:50,300
- What are you guys looking at?
- Oh, Aunt Bechay...

62
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:52,433
You're talking about me,
aren't you?

63
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:54,133
If you've nothing better to do,

64
00:02:54,267 --> 00:02:56,967
don't dip your toes
in other people's business!

65
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,233
That woman is something.

66
00:02:58,367 --> 00:03:00,433
I told you she'd get mad at us.

67
00:03:00,567 --> 00:03:01,400
Why?

68
00:03:01,533 --> 00:03:03,333
What I said is true!

69
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:05,267
Even if we don't have money,

70
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,500
I wouldn't take
that kind of work.

71
00:03:07,633 --> 00:03:09,567
Imagine showing my body
to random men?

72
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:11,133
I'd rather rummage
through trash!

73
00:03:11,267 --> 00:03:15,433
Diday, even if you expose
your body in front of men,

74
00:03:15,567 --> 00:03:16,900
no one will look at you!

75
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:18,300
- [SLAPS]
- [ALL] Ooh!

76
00:03:18,433 --> 00:03:20,700
If I find out you're going
to that bar,

77
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:22,700
I'll beat you up real good!

78
00:03:22,833 --> 00:03:23,933
- [BLOW LANDS]
- Oh!

79
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:25,900
Don't embarrass me
in front of them.

80
00:03:26,033 --> 00:03:28,200
- Relax, Diday.
- Diday, sit down, come on.

81
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:30,100
Keep the shots coming!

82
00:03:30,233 --> 00:03:31,300
- [CHUCKLES]
- [BOTTLES CLINKING]

83
00:03:31,433 --> 00:03:34,300
Don't make her mad.

84
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:38,600
[FAINT CHATTER IN DISTANCE]

85
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:44,033
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

86
00:03:45,667 --> 00:03:52,867
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

87
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,767
[GABO INHALES DEEPLY]

88
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,467
Pa...

89
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:11,800
I'm not sure if I'm the one
who should be telling you this.

90
00:04:15,767 --> 00:04:17,067
[GABO INHALES DEEPLY]

91
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:19,400
But I just wish...

92
00:04:24,633 --> 00:04:27,433
you didn't allow
Auntie Betchay to work

93
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,567
in Uncle Paquito's beerhouse.

94
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:34,067
It's dangerous for her
to be there.

95
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,833
Django might get back at her.

96
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:41,700
We tried to stop her.

97
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:44,800
But that's what she wants.

98
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:48,600
She wouldn't take
the job there...

99
00:04:48,733 --> 00:04:50,267
if I hadn't gotten shot.

100
00:04:56,633 --> 00:04:58,833
It hurts seeing you hurt.

101
00:05:03,167 --> 00:05:04,367
This isn't right.

102
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:11,633
I can imagine what the men
around here think of you.

103
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,100
In the whole community.

104
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,733
But don't worry, Pa.

105
00:05:21,233 --> 00:05:23,300
Once I get a job...

106
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:28,100
we won't let her work
in a place like that anymore.

107
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,700
[RUDY BREATHES DEEPLY]

108
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:33,867
Thank you, son.

109
00:05:37,133 --> 00:05:38,100
But...

110
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,900
I am the man of the house.

111
00:05:42,767 --> 00:05:45,000
I should be the one working...

112
00:05:46,867 --> 00:05:49,333
to provide our family's needs.

113
00:05:51,833 --> 00:05:53,867
It's embarrassing
to admit but...

114
00:05:56,367 --> 00:05:59,133
your Auntie Betchay is the one
making money to provide for us.

115
00:06:00,867 --> 00:06:03,500
Ever since Betchay
and I got together,

116
00:06:04,467 --> 00:06:07,033
she has always been the one
doing everything

117
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,200
for this family.

118
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:09,767
[MUSIC TURNS SOFT]

119
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:10,867
And...

120
00:06:12,433 --> 00:06:13,567
she never left us behind.

121
00:06:15,367 --> 00:06:17,867
I'm very grateful for her.

122
00:06:19,033 --> 00:06:21,100
When we lost your mother,

123
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,900
I lost my way too.

124
00:06:30,067 --> 00:06:31,433
I forgot...

125
00:06:34,933 --> 00:06:36,767
I forgot I can find love again.

126
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:39,933
And your Auntie Betchay,

127
00:06:40,867 --> 00:06:42,200
she was just my friend.

128
00:06:43,433 --> 00:06:44,900
I didn't promise
anything to her.

129
00:06:45,033 --> 00:06:46,667
I couldn't give anything to her.

130
00:06:47,633 --> 00:06:48,667
But...

131
00:06:51,133 --> 00:06:53,000
whatever happens,
she didn't leave us.

132
00:06:54,267 --> 00:06:55,400
You and I.

133
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:58,400
[FIRE CRACKLING]

134
00:06:58,533 --> 00:07:04,767
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

135
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:06,933
<i> Daddy.</i>

136
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:08,633
<i> Where are we?</i>

137
00:07:10,633 --> 00:07:12,067
<i> This is where I grew up.</i>

138
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:15,100
And this will be your new home.

139
00:07:18,033 --> 00:07:19,633
<i> Son, from now on,</i>

140
00:07:20,033 --> 00:07:21,700
<i> you'll call me Papa.</i>

141
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:23,433
<i> We've got to belong here.</i>

142
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,567
<i> Yes, Papa.</i>

143
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:26,700
<i> Let's go.</i>

144
00:07:26,833 --> 00:07:33,767
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

145
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,933
[YOUNG RUDY]<i> We'll move in here,
</i> son, with your Aunt Mameng.

146
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:39,833
<i> Rudy?</i>

147
00:07:40,667 --> 00:07:43,133
[SQUEALS] Oh, Rudy!

148
00:07:43,267 --> 00:07:46,267
<i> Rudy, it really is you!</i>

149
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:49,133
<i> What a surprise!</i>

150
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,133
<i> Oh my!</i>

151
00:07:50,267 --> 00:07:52,100
<i> You've been gone forever!</i>

152
00:07:52,233 --> 00:07:53,633
<i> Are you moving back here?</i>

153
00:07:53,767 --> 00:07:55,000
<i>Where have you been, anyway?
[SNIFFS]</i>

154
00:07:55,133 --> 00:07:56,067
<i> You smell so good!</i>

155
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,767
<i> Hey there, you little cutie!</i>

156
00:07:58,900 --> 00:07:59,900
<i> What's your name?</i>

157
00:08:00,033 --> 00:08:01,367
<i> I'm Gabriel.</i>

158
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,000
<i> Gabriel.</i>

159
00:08:03,133 --> 00:08:06,600
[GIGGLES] You look so handsome,
just like your father.

160
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:08,400
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

161
00:08:08,533 --> 00:08:09,600
<i> Where's your mother?</i>

162
00:08:11,333 --> 00:08:12,933
<i> She's dead.</i>

163
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:22,433
<i> Rudy?</i>

164
00:08:22,933 --> 00:08:26,933
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

165
00:08:27,067 --> 00:08:28,100
<i> Rudy!</i>

166
00:08:28,233 --> 00:08:29,900
<i> - Big sis.
<i> -</i> [YOUNG MAMENG]<i> Oh my...</i></i>

167
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:32,600
<i> This is Gabriel, my son.</i>

168
00:08:33,933 --> 00:08:35,300
<i> Gabriel.</i>

169
00:08:35,867 --> 00:08:36,833
<i> Such a handsome boy.</i>

170
00:08:36,967 --> 00:08:38,767
<i> Come on, let's head inside.</i>

171
00:08:39,167 --> 00:08:40,400
<i>- Follow me.
- That's your Aunt Mameng.</i>

172
00:08:40,533 --> 00:08:41,533
[YOUNG MAMENG EXHALES]

173
00:08:42,033 --> 00:08:45,567
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:47,133
- [GLASS THUDS]
<i> - Dinner's ready.</i>

175
00:08:47,933 --> 00:08:49,967
<i>I brought something
to go with your drink.</i>

176
00:08:50,233 --> 00:08:51,267
<i> Chicken intestines.</i>

177
00:08:51,967 --> 00:08:53,233
<i> Three skewers of them.</i>

178
00:08:53,367 --> 00:08:54,200
[GIGGLES]

179
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:55,733
<i> Here.</i>

180
00:08:58,233 --> 00:08:59,833
<i> The little one's asleep now.</i>

181
00:09:01,367 --> 00:09:02,200
<i> Where's Mameng?</i>

182
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:03,367
<i> She's away.</i>

183
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:04,700
<i> She went to Cebu.</i>

184
00:09:05,133 --> 00:09:06,167
[YOUNG BETCHAY] Hmm.

185
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:08,000
<i> What's that?</i>

186
00:09:08,133 --> 00:09:10,533
<i>I thought this would be
the turning point in my life.</i>

187
00:09:14,267 --> 00:09:16,233
- What exactly happened to you?
- [ZIPPER RASPS]

188
00:09:17,933 --> 00:09:20,733
<i>You didn't come home
for eight years.</i>

189
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:22,900
- [BOTTLE SCRAPES]
- [ALCOHOL SLOSHING]

190
00:09:23,033 --> 00:09:24,733
<i>I don't want
to discuss it, Betchay.</i>

191
00:09:25,367 --> 00:09:26,900
<i>I'd rather not
remember the past.</i>

192
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:28,533
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

193
00:09:28,633 --> 00:09:30,467
Rudy, how can I be there for you

194
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:33,200
<i>if you won't share
what you've gone through?</i>

195
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:36,400
<i>Let's just say that I thought
I had finally struck luck.</i>

196
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:39,933
<i> That my life had changed.</i>

197
00:09:40,967 --> 00:09:42,033
<i> But no.</i>

198
00:09:42,167 --> 00:09:43,667
<i> No, I was still cursed.</i>

199
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,300
<i> I lost everything.</i>

200
00:09:45,433 --> 00:09:48,100
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

201
00:09:48,233 --> 00:09:50,700
<i>You have to work hard
for things in life.</i>

202
00:09:51,233 --> 00:09:53,967
<i>Not everything can be left
to luck.</i>

203
00:09:54,467 --> 00:09:58,467
<i>But if you feel like
you've lost it all...</i>

204
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:02,167
Rudy, you can still start again.

205
00:10:02,333 --> 00:10:04,000
<i> How can I start over, Betchay?</i>

206
00:10:04,967 --> 00:10:06,767
All I know is being a mechanic.

207
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
[CHAIR SCRAPING]

208
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,633
<i> Rudy...</i>

209
00:10:10,767 --> 00:10:12,900
<i> How about we work together?</i>

210
00:10:13,033 --> 00:10:14,800
<i> I have money.</i>

211
00:10:15,233 --> 00:10:17,233
<i> I can give you capital.</i>

212
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,867
<i>Let's make
all your dreams happen.</i>

213
00:10:20,333 --> 00:10:22,000
<i> Didn't you want a repair shop?</i>

214
00:10:22,133 --> 00:10:23,633
<i> I'll give you one.</i>

215
00:10:23,767 --> 00:10:27,033
<i>I know someone who owns
a house with a big yard.</i>

216
00:10:27,167 --> 00:10:28,033
<i> We can set it up there.</i>

217
00:10:28,167 --> 00:10:29,533
<i> I'll help you.</i>

218
00:10:29,667 --> 00:10:36,567
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

219
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:40,700
[GLASS THUDS]

220
00:10:41,367 --> 00:10:42,200
[DOOR OPENS]

221
00:10:42,333 --> 00:10:43,300
<i> Hi!</i>

222
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:45,500
<i>- Hi, Betchay!
- Where's your father?</i>

223
00:10:45,633 --> 00:10:46,567
<i> He's not around.</i>

224
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:47,767
<i> Oh, really?</i>

225
00:10:48,733 --> 00:10:49,767
[YOUNG BETCHAY] Ah.

226
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,200
<i> What's that?</i>

227
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,567
<i>A dish for your
good-looking father!</i>

228
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:57,733
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:10:57,867 --> 00:10:59,267
<i> It smells delicious!</i>

230
00:11:00,167 --> 00:11:01,667
<i> You're hungry, huh?</i>

231
00:11:02,167 --> 00:11:03,100
[GIGGLES]

232
00:11:03,233 --> 00:11:04,167
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

233
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:06,267
<i> Alright, dig in.</i>

234
00:11:09,533 --> 00:11:10,367
[YOUNG BETCHAY GIGGLES]

235
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:11,533
<i> What's this?</i>

236
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,133
<i> Leftover food.</i>

237
00:11:13,467 --> 00:11:15,400
<i>So tasty,
just like fried chicken!</i>

238
00:11:15,533 --> 00:11:17,467
<i>It's our specialty here
in Tondo.</i>

239
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,133
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

240
00:11:19,267 --> 00:11:20,467
<i>- Hey...
- Mmm!</i>

241
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,633
<i> Do you have any rice?</i>

242
00:11:21,767 --> 00:11:22,967
<i> Wait, let me check.</i>

243
00:11:25,467 --> 00:11:27,867
<i>Hey, Gabriel, leave some
for your father, alright?</i>

244
00:11:28,933 --> 00:11:29,967
<i> Rudy?</i>

245
00:11:31,133 --> 00:11:33,867
<i>Come on now, Rudy.
Get up.</i>

246
00:11:34,233 --> 00:11:35,367
<i> Sit properly.</i>

247
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:36,767
<i> Rudy, please...</i>

248
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:38,733
- [YOUNG BETCHAY SIGHING]
- [GRUNTS]

249
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:40,767
<i>- What's the matter with you?
- [SIGHS]</i>

250
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,567
<i> Come on.</i>

251
00:11:43,067 --> 00:11:44,767
Rudy, what's happening with you?

252
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:45,867
[GULPING]

253
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,100
<i>Do you want your son
to see you like this?</i>

254
00:11:48,967 --> 00:11:50,267
<i> You're always drunk.</i>

255
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:52,367
There's a child living here too.

256
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:53,400
[YOUNG RUDY SIGHS]

257
00:11:53,533 --> 00:11:55,333
<i>Rudy, my love,
I'm sorry, but...</i>

258
00:11:55,467 --> 00:11:59,700
<i>...no amount of drinking
will bring your wife back.</i>

259
00:11:59,833 --> 00:12:01,600
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:12:01,733 --> 00:12:02,767
<i> That's enough.</i>

261
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:04,033
<i> Stop. Give me that.</i>

262
00:12:04,167 --> 00:12:05,000
<i> It's over.</i>

263
00:12:05,133 --> 00:12:06,233
<i> Let's get you to bed.</i>

264
00:12:06,367 --> 00:12:07,867
<i>- I want...
- No, you can't.</i>

265
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,100
<i> Rudy-- Oh my!</i>

266
00:12:09,833 --> 00:12:10,833
<i> Rudy!</i>

267
00:12:11,167 --> 00:12:12,167
<i> Oh my!</i>

268
00:12:12,633 --> 00:12:13,633
<i> Rudy, wait--</i>

269
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:15,667
- [HEAVY THUD]
- [RUDY BREATHES DEEPLY]

270
00:12:15,833 --> 00:12:17,067
[VOICE SHAKING] Rudy...

271
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,700
<i> Whatever happened in the past,</i>

272
00:12:19,833 --> 00:12:21,700
<i> forget it.</i>

273
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,467
<i> It's already behind you.</i>

274
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:28,967
<i> Set yourself free.</i>

275
00:12:31,467 --> 00:12:33,933
<i>There are so many people
who love you.</i>

276
00:12:35,133 --> 00:12:36,633
<i> No matter how much we want it,</i>

277
00:12:36,767 --> 00:12:39,933
<i>it won't change the fact that
your wife is gone.</i>

278
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:43,167
<i>No one can ever replace
Belinda in my heart.</i>

279
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:52,200
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:12:53,367 --> 00:12:54,433
[SNIFFLES]

281
00:12:55,633 --> 00:12:56,833
[YOUNG RUDY] No one...

282
00:12:56,967 --> 00:12:58,133
[YOUNG BETCHAY
BREATHES SHAKINGLY]

283
00:12:58,267 --> 00:12:59,600
[YOUNG RUNDY WHIMPERS]
<i> No one...</i>

284
00:13:01,233 --> 00:13:03,567
- [CRYING QUIETLY]
<i> - No one...</i>

285
00:13:04,767 --> 00:13:07,200
<i> I'll help you.</i>

286
00:13:08,567 --> 00:13:09,633
[BREATHES DEEPLY, SNIFFLES]

287
00:13:09,767 --> 00:13:12,433
I've loved you for a long time.

288
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,433
- [MUMBLING]
- [SNIFFLES]

289
00:13:15,067 --> 00:13:17,533
<i> Let me help you.</i>

290
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:21,267
<i>I'll do anything
to make you love me.</i>

291
00:13:22,033 --> 00:13:27,967
[SNIFFLING]

292
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:31,367
- [GRUNTS]
- [SNIFFLES]

293
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:32,567
[YOUNG RUDY SIGHS]

294
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:36,467
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

295
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:37,633
[YOUNG RUDY GROANS SOFTLY]

296
00:13:42,867 --> 00:13:43,933
[SNIFFLES]

297
00:13:44,733 --> 00:13:46,300
<i> I love you.</i>

298
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:57,800
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

299
00:13:57,967 --> 00:13:58,967
[SNIFFLES]

300
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:01,167
I know all of that, Pa.

301
00:14:04,667 --> 00:14:07,667
I know it was Aunt Betchay
who hustled

302
00:14:09,133 --> 00:14:10,800
to provide for us.

303
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,133
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

304
00:14:14,267 --> 00:14:16,900
And I witnessed...

305
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,467
how hurt you were
when Mama died.

306
00:14:30,467 --> 00:14:31,600
But, Pa...

307
00:14:33,867 --> 00:14:35,667
Don't be discouraged.

308
00:14:37,367 --> 00:14:39,367
Don't lose hope.

309
00:14:41,467 --> 00:14:43,667
I'm here to help you.

310
00:14:45,967 --> 00:14:47,133
I know, Gabo.

311
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,967
Nothing can compare
to my love for your mother.

312
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:58,367
I've made many wrong decisions
and countless mistakes.

313
00:15:00,867 --> 00:15:03,733
But I only did
all those things...

314
00:15:04,633 --> 00:15:06,700
...to give you a good life.

315
00:15:07,833 --> 00:15:09,300
I just hope, son...

316
00:15:10,633 --> 00:15:11,967
one day...

317
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:14,900
I hope you find...

318
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:20,700
a woman who will truly love you
and change your life.

319
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:26,033
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

320
00:15:26,033 --> 00:15:27,500
[SNIFFLES]

321
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,067
[SIGHS]

322
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:30,767
[SNIFFLES]

323
00:15:31,567 --> 00:15:34,533
Why are you suddenly so quiet?

324
00:15:34,533 --> 00:15:39,400
Have you found someone?
Someone who will love you?

325
00:15:40,367 --> 00:15:42,733
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

326
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:46,933
Not yet, Pa.

327
00:15:48,267 --> 00:15:50,133
And that's not on my mind
right now.

328
00:15:53,367 --> 00:15:54,833
All I want right now...

329
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:58,833
...is to improve our lives
and help you.

330
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:03,867
But if ever I find
a woman to love,

331
00:16:06,367 --> 00:16:08,067
I want to be like you.

332
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:12,800
Because I saw how much
affection you had for Mama,

333
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,267
how you took care of her,

334
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,000
and how you made us
feel loved.

335
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:25,700
I really look up to you
as a father.

336
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,667
As a parent.

337
00:16:29,933 --> 00:16:31,700
I love you so much, Pa.

338
00:16:33,533 --> 00:16:35,200
I love you so much.

339
00:16:36,767 --> 00:16:39,233
[SNIFFLES]

340
00:16:39,233 --> 00:16:46,100
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

341
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:53,800
Hey, make sure that's clean.

342
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:56,667
And arrange the chairs.
It looks like a mess right now.

343
00:16:56,667 --> 00:16:58,667
And you four!

344
00:16:58,667 --> 00:17:00,167
Once a customer comes in,

345
00:17:00,167 --> 00:17:02,400
offer food and drinks
right away.

346
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:04,267
Make sure they will order.

347
00:17:04,267 --> 00:17:07,167
Hey, Betchay!
Why are you late?

348
00:17:07,167 --> 00:17:09,400
- Uh...
- Wow, Betchay.

349
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:11,067
You just got here,

350
00:17:11,067 --> 00:17:13,567
but you're looking like
you're ready for closing time.

351
00:17:13,567 --> 00:17:16,767
Sorry. Rudy and I had a spat.
That's why I'm late.

352
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:18,833
Well, don't bring
your personal problems here.

353
00:17:18,833 --> 00:17:21,267
Yeah! That's bad for business!

354
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,200
- True.
- Betchay.

355
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,200
Our customers here

356
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:29,833
are mostly jeepney drivers
and construction workers.

357
00:17:29,833 --> 00:17:33,233
They work themselves to
the bone every day.

358
00:17:33,233 --> 00:17:37,067
Yes, that's why we must
entertain them

359
00:17:37,067 --> 00:17:39,233
and help them
relieve their stress.

360
00:17:39,233 --> 00:17:41,333
Well, sorry.
I'm sorry, okay?

361
00:17:41,333 --> 00:17:44,433
Keep in mind, Betchay,
that you're just new here.

362
00:17:44,433 --> 00:17:46,733
So, you must prove yourself.

363
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:49,367
And you have a deal
with Boss Paquito, right?

364
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:52,700
If you bring in money, he'd let
you keep working here.

365
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:53,967
- Remember?
- Yes, yes.

366
00:17:53,967 --> 00:17:57,200
So, can you forget about
your problem with Rudy

367
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,967
even just for tonight?
Can you do that?

368
00:17:59,967 --> 00:18:01,967
- Well, you have to.
- Yeah.

369
00:18:01,967 --> 00:18:04,367
Smile and show off
your cleavage

370
00:18:04,367 --> 00:18:05,767
so you can attract customers.

371
00:18:07,267 --> 00:18:12,867
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

372
00:18:12,867 --> 00:18:14,433
How's your father doing?

373
00:18:17,267 --> 00:18:18,600
He's fine now.

374
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,600
I can't believe Betchay.
What was she thinking?

375
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,067
[MAMENG]
She's so stubborn.

376
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:27,367
What should we do to stop her
from working at that bar?

377
00:18:29,133 --> 00:18:34,967
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:18:34,967 --> 00:18:36,533
I don't know, Auntie.

379
00:18:44,267 --> 00:18:50,033
[UPBEAT BAR MUSIC
BLARING ON SPEAKERS]

380
00:18:50,033 --> 00:18:52,433
- Hi! Hello!
- Good evening!

381
00:18:52,433 --> 00:18:53,833
Want to sit by the electric fan?

382
00:18:53,833 --> 00:18:55,833
The lighting over there
makes me extra pretty.

383
00:18:55,867 --> 00:18:57,600
Just one bottle? Make it two!

384
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,400
- Alright. I'll have two.
- Two beers, please!

385
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:00,867
I'll have a bottle, too.

386
00:19:00,867 --> 00:19:04,967
See that wench?
She's stealing our customers!

387
00:19:04,967 --> 00:19:08,467
It seems she's no longer upset.
Good thing she listened to us.

388
00:19:08,467 --> 00:19:10,367
- Ugh!
- She must really need money.

389
00:19:10,367 --> 00:19:11,967
[CUSTOMER]
I really love drinking with you!

390
00:19:11,967 --> 00:19:14,700
Me, too!
You're so cute! [GIGGLING]

391
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:17,867
- Give us another bucket!
- Order some bar chow too.

392
00:19:17,867 --> 00:19:19,667
We have a special promo.

393
00:19:19,667 --> 00:19:21,367
[CUSTOMER]
I'll have some bar chow too!

394
00:19:21,367 --> 00:19:25,367
- Bar chow for this table!
- [GIGGLING]

395
00:19:25,367 --> 00:19:27,567
- Drink up!
- Betchay...

396
00:19:27,567 --> 00:19:32,200
Take it easy on the alcohol.
It's too early to get drunk.

397
00:19:32,233 --> 00:19:34,467
You're only on
your first customer.

398
00:19:34,467 --> 00:19:36,667
- I can handle it. [GIGGLES]
- Really? [FORCED LAUGHTER]

399
00:19:36,667 --> 00:19:38,767
- Cheers!
- Oh! Okay!

400
00:19:38,767 --> 00:19:40,833
- Sir, enjoy!
- Cheers!

401
00:19:40,833 --> 00:19:42,767
- Enjoy.
- Let's drink our hearts out!

402
00:19:42,767 --> 00:19:46,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

403
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:50,533
Boss, am I really going
to follow what's in the script?

404
00:19:50,667 --> 00:19:52,800
Just tell them that a group
of men went after you

405
00:19:52,933 --> 00:19:55,233
-because you exposed the police!
- And then what?

406
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,733
I beat them all up?

407
00:19:57,867 --> 00:20:01,767
Yeah! Follow it up by saying
that you studied wushu,

408
00:20:01,933 --> 00:20:03,933
<i> taekwondo,</i> or wrestling!

409
00:20:04,067 --> 00:20:08,267
Say that you're a black belter
with a black eye too!

410
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:11,067
[ARNEL CLEARS THROAT]
Here. Use this.

411
00:20:12,033 --> 00:20:13,000
Looks cool.

412
00:20:13,133 --> 00:20:16,867
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

413
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,800
[ARNEL] There you go!

414
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:20,233
Perfect!

415
00:20:20,367 --> 00:20:22,267
Challenge all those villains

416
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:24,600
and ask them, "How much
is your dignity?"

417
00:20:24,733 --> 00:20:26,433
[LAUGHING] Boss.

418
00:20:26,567 --> 00:20:28,133
Salvador...

419
00:20:28,267 --> 00:20:31,767
[IN UNISON] The Avenger is here!

420
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:35,200
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [CLACKS]

421
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:37,400
[SALVADOR]<i> Salvador
</i> "The Avenger" Manalo.

422
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:38,933
<i> Protector of the oppressed.</i>

423
00:20:39,067 --> 00:20:41,400
[ACTION MUSIC PLAYING]

424
00:20:41,533 --> 00:20:43,233
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [THUDS]

425
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:46,167
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [GUN COCKS]

426
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:50,533
[ACTION MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

427
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:51,933
[CHAIR CLATTERS]

428
00:20:53,567 --> 00:20:56,600
Until when do you plan on
being trampled over?

429
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:58,600
You are being abused
every single day!

430
00:20:58,733 --> 00:21:01,700
If you can't defend yourselves,

431
00:21:01,833 --> 00:21:04,200
if you're scared,
call out to me!

432
00:21:04,333 --> 00:21:06,767
Salvador, The Avenger!

433
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,467
The protector of the oppressed.

434
00:21:09,633 --> 00:21:10,967
Hurry up!

435
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,733
That should've been washed
ages ago!

436
00:21:12,867 --> 00:21:14,900
- Quick, get out there!
- Sweetie!

437
00:21:15,233 --> 00:21:16,833
- What?
- Check this out!

438
00:21:16,967 --> 00:21:18,333
- What is it?
- Just look at it!

439
00:21:18,467 --> 00:21:20,033
- Huh?
- Look at it!

440
00:21:20,533 --> 00:21:22,600
[SALVADOR] The demolition
issue at Ginintuang Lupa

441
00:21:22,733 --> 00:21:24,700
<i>is making a lot of noise.
I followed it closely!</i>

442
00:21:24,833 --> 00:21:26,500
<i> A group of men ambushed me.</i>

443
00:21:26,633 --> 00:21:28,500
I just know that General Jacinto
<i> and the police</i>

444
00:21:28,633 --> 00:21:29,967
<i> sent them to attack me.</i>

445
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:32,500
That Salvador is blabbering
his mouth again!

446
00:21:32,633 --> 00:21:35,367
You know what to do.
I'll leave it to you.

447
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:38,100
Huh? What do you mean
you'll leave it to me?

448
00:21:38,233 --> 00:21:39,800
- What exactly are you leaving?
- Huh?

449
00:21:39,933 --> 00:21:41,500
Didn't Ma'am Isobel mention it?

450
00:21:41,667 --> 00:21:44,367
If we acquired new information,
we should report it immediately.

451
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,933
Then let's go together!

452
00:21:46,067 --> 00:21:48,700
So that if they turn violent
because of so much anger,

453
00:21:48,833 --> 00:21:50,800
- they'll strangle you first.
- Huh?

454
00:21:50,933 --> 00:21:52,967
- Go, lead the way! Go!
- Huh? You go first!

455
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:54,333
[TOTO WHISPERING] Hurry!

456
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:56,800
Wh-- where did they go?

457
00:21:57,367 --> 00:21:59,767
Oh, over there!
Quick, wave at her!

458
00:21:59,900 --> 00:22:01,600
- Get her attention!
- [WHISPERING] Ma'am!

459
00:22:01,733 --> 00:22:03,167
[TWINKLE] Psst! Ma'am!

460
00:22:04,267 --> 00:22:05,200
[TWINKLE] Ma'am!

461
00:22:05,333 --> 00:22:08,600
[QUIRKY STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

462
00:22:08,733 --> 00:22:10,900
Excuse me for a bit.
I'll be back.

463
00:22:11,033 --> 00:22:13,100
[TWINKLE PANTING]

464
00:22:13,233 --> 00:22:16,033
What is it? It's like you're
drowning from all that waving!

465
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:18,700
Didn't you and sir tell us
to give you an update

466
00:22:18,833 --> 00:22:20,867
when you're being called out?
Well, here it is!

467
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,700
- Huh? Right now?
- Yes!

468
00:22:22,833 --> 00:22:25,067
But I think it's better
if you check it yourselves.

469
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,400
[ISOBEL] What? Right now?

470
00:22:26,533 --> 00:22:27,900
- Yes, ma'am?
- I don't want to!

471
00:22:28,033 --> 00:22:29,100
What's the commotion about?

472
00:22:29,233 --> 00:22:30,667
- What's that?
- [TWINKLE] Watch it--

473
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:32,367
Ma'am, uh...

474
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:33,867
Is it something I need to see?
Give it here!

475
00:22:34,633 --> 00:22:35,633
Sir--

476
00:22:35,767 --> 00:22:37,033
[TOTO SIGHS]

477
00:22:37,167 --> 00:22:38,500
- Sir...
- [RICARDO SIGHS]

478
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:40,433
[SALVADOR] This morning,

479
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:43,867
<i> a group of men ambushed me.</i>

480
00:22:44,633 --> 00:22:46,333
<i>I have a feeling they want
to get rid of me</i>

481
00:22:46,467 --> 00:22:51,167
<i>because I called out
Ricardo Jacinto and the police</i>

482
00:22:51,333 --> 00:22:53,833
<i>regarding the demolishment
at Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

483
00:22:53,967 --> 00:22:59,000
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

484
00:22:59,133 --> 00:23:00,200
<i> What happened?</i>

485
00:23:00,333 --> 00:23:02,133
<i> Their threats</i>

486
00:23:02,267 --> 00:23:03,633
didn't work on me!

487
00:23:03,767 --> 00:23:05,033
Here, watch this.

488
00:23:05,167 --> 00:23:06,500
[BLOWS LANDING]

489
00:23:06,633 --> 00:23:08,767
[SALVADOR]<i> What now, huh?
</i> See that?

490
00:23:08,900 --> 00:23:13,233
<i>There were so many of them
but they're no match for me!</i>

491
00:23:13,367 --> 00:23:14,500
<i> Why is that?</i>

492
00:23:14,633 --> 00:23:18,200
I studied five kinds of martial
<i> arts. Five!</i>

493
00:23:18,333 --> 00:23:21,133
<i> So listen up, you dogs.</i>

494
00:23:21,267 --> 00:23:23,967
Even the person
who ordered you to do this.

495
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:27,767
You'll regret letting me live.

496
00:23:28,567 --> 00:23:32,467
I'll be the one to put an end
to your depravity!

497
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:34,100
You bastards!

498
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:41,067
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

499
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:43,667
Your timing is perfect,
isn't it?

500
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:46,833
But Ma'am, if we don't tell you
right away, you get mad.

501
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:47,833
You blame us!

502
00:23:47,967 --> 00:23:49,133
- Blame Salvador instead!
- Get out!

503
00:23:49,267 --> 00:23:50,633
- Yes, ma'am!
- [TWINKLE SCREAMING]

504
00:23:52,467 --> 00:23:53,633
[CLEARS THROAT]

505
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:55,833
[CATALAN] Ricardo,

506
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,367
looks like that reporter got you
in a spot.

507
00:23:58,500 --> 00:24:00,500
The project seems to be less
and less possible.

508
00:24:00,933 --> 00:24:03,167
Well, it's 'cause
the project is rich.

509
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:04,667
That's why they keep
going after it.

510
00:24:05,133 --> 00:24:06,233
But I assure you,

511
00:24:07,367 --> 00:24:08,467
we don't have a problem.

512
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:10,933
It's not very enticing
to invest in you right now.

513
00:24:11,067 --> 00:24:12,600
As more time passes by,

514
00:24:12,733 --> 00:24:16,000
people will believe that
reporter more than your vision.

515
00:24:16,133 --> 00:24:17,433
You're successful
in your career,

516
00:24:17,567 --> 00:24:18,833
but not in business.

517
00:24:18,967 --> 00:24:25,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

518
00:24:31,233 --> 00:24:32,867
Wait a minute.

519
00:24:32,867 --> 00:24:34,900
Isn't this a reunion?

520
00:24:34,900 --> 00:24:37,767
We shouldn't keep
talking about business.

521
00:24:38,367 --> 00:24:42,200
Why don't we relax
and talk about our families?

522
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:43,733
- Ah, yes!
- Yes.

523
00:24:43,733 --> 00:24:45,767
- Good idea.
- Yes. Okay.

524
00:24:45,767 --> 00:24:47,933
- Have a seat!
- This is a good distraction.

525
00:24:47,933 --> 00:24:49,033
- [LAUGHTER]
- Yes!

526
00:24:49,033 --> 00:24:50,900
- Let's have some cheese.
- Vic.

527
00:24:50,900 --> 00:24:51,900
Yes?

528
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:53,567
How are you children doing?

529
00:24:53,567 --> 00:24:56,500
My daughter has been
a surgeon for 10 years.

530
00:24:56,500 --> 00:24:58,800
My son, on the other hand,
is a regional court judge.

531
00:24:58,800 --> 00:25:00,900
It's nice that they are
still here in the country.

532
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:04,900
After studying abroad, my
three kids won't come back home.

533
00:25:04,933 --> 00:25:06,933
They say they don't see
a future in the Philippines.

534
00:25:06,933 --> 00:25:08,233
That might not be the case.

535
00:25:09,033 --> 00:25:10,067
Look at the father,

536
00:25:10,067 --> 00:25:12,533
a highly decorated
and respected general.

537
00:25:12,533 --> 00:25:14,933
- Yes.
- Very influential.

538
00:25:14,933 --> 00:25:16,533
They would have
never had it so easy.

539
00:25:16,533 --> 00:25:18,133
[MAN] That's the problem.

540
00:25:18,133 --> 00:25:21,033
I always had to fly around
the world just to see them.

541
00:25:21,033 --> 00:25:22,567
- I move around a lot.
- Wow!

542
00:25:22,567 --> 00:25:25,600
In London, in Dubai,
and even in New Jersey.

543
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:27,300
- Wow!
- Wow!

544
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:28,467
Poor you.

545
00:25:28,467 --> 00:25:30,633
That seems like such
a huge problem.

546
00:25:30,633 --> 00:25:33,400
Our children know
how easy life becomes

547
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:34,967
once you become
a police officer.

548
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:37,667
My son is following
in my footsteps.

549
00:25:37,667 --> 00:25:39,600
- He's already a Colonel.
- Good for you.

550
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:40,967
What about your son, Ricardo?

551
00:25:41,567 --> 00:25:44,533
He would surely hold
a high rank by now.

552
00:25:44,533 --> 00:25:51,533
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

553
00:25:52,500 --> 00:25:53,833
I wish.

554
00:25:56,333 --> 00:25:57,933
I focused my attention
on him back then.

555
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,500
I really felt he had
what it takes.

556
00:26:03,900 --> 00:26:05,267
I thought he might
be the next...

557
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,400
Jacinto, chief of police.

558
00:26:12,700 --> 00:26:14,067
But he was taken too early.

559
00:26:14,067 --> 00:26:20,933
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

560
00:26:20,933 --> 00:26:21,967
Ah.

561
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:25,800
But we have a daughter
who is a police officer!

562
00:26:28,300 --> 00:26:31,233
Oh, look, she's right here!

563
00:26:31,433 --> 00:26:33,767
- What's happening?
- [ISOBEL] Your dad's reunion.

564
00:26:33,767 --> 00:26:36,467
A reunion
with his general friends!

565
00:26:36,467 --> 00:26:38,000
- Auntie Vicky, hi!
- Hello.

566
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:40,200
- Hello! Hi, everybody!
- Hi!

567
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,533
Hi everyone.
Good evening.

568
00:26:42,767 --> 00:26:44,033
Well, gentlemen,

569
00:26:44,033 --> 00:26:46,767
this is my eldest daughter,
Max

570
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:49,133
- [ISOBEL] Yes.
- One hell of a cop.

571
00:26:50,267 --> 00:26:51,600
- Can I tell them about it?
- [MAX] Oh!

572
00:26:51,933 --> 00:26:53,400
Earlier this year,

573
00:26:53,833 --> 00:26:55,100
over one weekend,

574
00:26:56,233 --> 00:26:59,200
she caught three people
on the most wanted list.

575
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:02,133
- Good job!
- Wow!

576
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:06,233
The only question
I have is...

577
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:09,833
is she good or is she good?

578
00:27:10,167 --> 00:27:11,367
Lieutenant,

579
00:27:11,367 --> 00:27:14,567
I see you're following
your father's footsteps.

580
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,100
[CHUCKLES]

581
00:27:17,100 --> 00:27:18,700
I'll try doing that, sir.

582
00:27:18,700 --> 00:27:20,533
I'm sure
you will make him proud.

583
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:22,567
What do you mean
he will?

584
00:27:23,033 --> 00:27:24,667
- [MAN] Yeah.- She will?

585
00:27:25,267 --> 00:27:28,400
I'm already proud of her.

586
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:30,100
- Aww.
- Aww.

587
00:27:31,867 --> 00:27:34,167
- [MAX] Thank you.
- Cheers!

588
00:27:34,167 --> 00:27:35,767
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

589
00:27:41,100 --> 00:27:43,967
[TEKLA] We should've
went here earlier.

590
00:27:43,967 --> 00:27:45,467
[WOMAN] You should've
went here instead!

591
00:27:45,467 --> 00:27:46,700
[TEKLA] I know! They fought
with someone instead.

592
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:48,167
[IPE] You should've
told us earlier.

593
00:27:48,167 --> 00:27:50,033
- [BINOY] He peeked at them.
- [TEKLA] Who started it?

594
00:27:50,467 --> 00:27:52,133
See? I knew it.

595
00:27:52,133 --> 00:27:53,367
Gabo!

596
00:27:53,367 --> 00:27:54,300
Have a seat?

597
00:27:54,300 --> 00:27:55,833
- Let him sit.
- What happened?

598
00:27:56,567 --> 00:27:58,167
Why did Rudy
and Betchay fight?

599
00:27:58,867 --> 00:28:01,600
It's because Aunt Bechay
is working at Paquito's bar.

600
00:28:02,200 --> 00:28:03,600
[DIDAY] I knew it!

601
00:28:03,600 --> 00:28:05,700
What Betchay did was wrong.

602
00:28:05,700 --> 00:28:06,900
What did Rudy say?

603
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,600
- Was he angry?
- [BONG] Of course he is!

604
00:28:09,600 --> 00:28:11,500
What sane man
would be happy

605
00:28:11,500 --> 00:28:13,167
that his wife's body is being
desired by other men?

606
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:15,767
[TOLITS] Gabo.

607
00:28:15,767 --> 00:28:18,467
I'm scared Betchay
might be in danger.

608
00:28:18,467 --> 00:28:20,167
Django might
use her for revenge.

609
00:28:20,167 --> 00:28:22,233
[DABOY] You need
to talk to her, Gabo.

610
00:28:25,767 --> 00:28:28,133
I don't know how
I'll talk to Aunt Betchay.

611
00:28:30,633 --> 00:28:32,200
But I can think of only one way.

612
00:28:33,667 --> 00:28:35,733
I needed to find a decent job

613
00:28:36,600 --> 00:28:38,067
So that I could support
my family.

614
00:28:38,933 --> 00:28:40,000
If I do that...

615
00:28:40,833 --> 00:28:43,700
Betchay doesn't have
to work at that bar anymore.

616
00:28:44,467 --> 00:28:46,300
If she stays there,
her life could be in danger.

617
00:28:50,300 --> 00:28:51,600
<i> I need everyone here.</i>

618
00:28:51,600 --> 00:28:53,333
<i> But I'll kill Mr. Chan.</i>

619
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:57,800
<i>This is your chance to get rid
of Samantha Jacinto, Lucas.</i>

620
00:28:57,833 --> 00:28:59,200
<i>Do you think what
you've done will be forgotten?</i>

621
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:00,733
<i>Do you think they'll
remove your suspension?</i>

622
00:29:00,733 --> 00:29:02,733
<i>That you'll remove the stain
you've done in my name?</i>

623
00:29:02,733 --> 00:29:04,833
<i>You didn't just bring shame
in this family,</i>

624
00:29:04,833 --> 00:29:06,833
<i>you also brought us
so much pain.</i>

625
00:29:06,833 --> 00:29:09,733
<i>We are all devastated
over losing our brother!</i>

626
00:29:09,733 --> 00:29:13,900
<i>I pray everyday hoping
that you'll forgive me.</i>

627
00:29:13,900 --> 00:29:16,733
<i>Sometimes I wish
it was you who died.</i>

628
00:29:16,733 --> 00:29:19,400
<i> My husband, Babot, was taken!</i>

629
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:22,733
<i> They took my father, Gabo!</i>

630
00:29:22,733 --> 00:29:25,633
<i> I promise you we'll find him.</i>

631
00:29:25,633 --> 00:29:27,400
<i> So this is what you're doing
to these men!</i>

632
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:28,567
<i> You're using them
for business!</i>

633
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:30,200
<i>There's nothing
you can do because</i>

634
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,900
<i> we'll slaughter you alive!</i>
